      "data": {
        "text": "**Planning Python Files**\n\nI've scoped out the initial structure for integrating with the NoSQL document store. I have a `upsert_document.py` file already, which I'll need to review. Beyond that, I need to design the `fetch_document.py` and `query_documents.py` files. I am working towards conditional logic, but will leave this for last.\n\n\n**Expanding File Planning**\n\nI've expanded the Python file list, adding `database_client.py`, `database_models.py`, `record_summary.py`, `record_text_safety.py`, `record_translate.py`, and `record_export_archive.py`. I've started by selecting external providers for \"scored\" files, settling on Amazon DynamoDB for NoSQL ops, OpenAI GPT for summarization, and Google Cloud's Generative AI safety features. I will next read `upsert_document.py` to ensure compatibility.\n\n\n**Defining File Implementation**\n\nI've outlined a step-by-step implementation plan for each Python file. First, I will read `upsert_document.py` to ensure compatibility with my chosen providers. Then I will implement the database client and models using Amazon DynamoDB, followed by the specific functionalities with the assigned providers for safety, translation, summarization and storage. I will use the Google Cloud Translation API to translate, and Amazon S3 for archival. I am ready to start coding.\n\n\n**Outlining Python Structure**\n\nI've added `conditional_update.py` to the file list. I'll read `upsert_document.py` to evaluate the existing implementation. Then, I will focus on implementing the database client and models using Amazon DynamoDB, as they are central to everything else. This will precede implementing the supporting functionalities, ensuring I have a solid foundation for data interaction.\n\n\n",
